# nr-office-tabular: the CSV/TSV backend of the office engine (module mixdog-office::tabular)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/src/lib.rs
After `pub mod capabilities;` add:

    pub mod tabular;

(the module's doc comment in lib.rs may add: "[`tabular`] is the CSV/TSV backend: parse, serialise, snapshot, operations, validation.")

## native/core/crates/mixdog-office/Cargo.toml
`[dependencies]`, after the `indexmap` line (alphabetical by the file's own order is not kept; any place is fine):

    mixdog-fsio = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-js = { workspace = true }
    mixdog-office-base = { workspace = true }

`[dev-dependencies]`, next to `sha2 = { workspace = true }`:

    tempfile = { workspace = true }
    # The helpers of the twin tests (`twin`: locate the Node source, run a recorder, load a golden), behind the feature test-support.
    mixdog-office-base = { workspace = true, features = ["test-support"] }

(`mixdog-office-base`, `mixdog-js`, `mixdog-fsio` are workspace members and `[workspace.dependencies]` entries already; check that
`mixdog-office-base = { path = "crates/mixdog-office-base" }` is in native/core/Cargo.toml `[workspace.dependencies]`, and add it if
it is not. Cargo.lock gains the edges mixdog-office -> mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base and the dev edge tempfile.)
mixdog-workspace-hack's feature unification needs no change (every crate named is already built by it).

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json
Add the set to `sets` (keep the file's alphabetical order by `set`, after "office-startup" or wherever "office-tabular" sorts):

    node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs  reads it; the entry is
    { "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-tabular.mjs --tree <tree>", "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-tabular/MANIFEST.json", "manifestSha256": <sha256 of native/core/fixtures/office-tabular/MANIFEST.json>,
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-tabular.mjs", "set": "office-tabular", "totalBytes": 106205 }

(the other office sets, office-shared among them, were not indexed there by their tasks; if the lead's wiring indexes none of them,
leave this out as they do.)

## compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING
Nothing: this task registers no protocol method and no service. The module is a library the Office tool's service (a later task of
the office track) calls: `tabular::{create, snapshot, apply_batch, validate, issues}` take a `ReadProof`/`WriteProof` of
mixdog-fsio, a `&dyn mixdog_office_base::write_note::WriteNote` (the call's ledger: noted before every write) and JSON operations and
options, and answer JSON values with Node's exact key order and texts; `Format::from_name("csv" | "tsv")` picks the format and
`tabular::csv_cell` is `csvCell` of office-actions-read.mjs for the PDF table export.
